{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789334588,"nonce":"rPfhdbASZFqKQ4V01G92QxtnZF8=","title":"Cranelift compiles a loop entry as a clone of the function","message":"Each OSR entry was its own function, lowered from the loop header over\neverything reachable from it, so a body with k loops cost k+1\nlowerings and compiles (bench/method_call.wren's module body: ~3.6k\nlines of CLIF for the body plus ~2.5k per entry). The two-stage\ncompile (body plus the hot entry first, the rest after the install)\nand the module-body stub existed to hide that cost, and the\ninterpreter still waited ~10 ms on the NUC for the first stage.\n\nNow one body carries every entry, the way the LLVM tier does: the\nfunction's entry block reads two request words the module owns (entry\nindex, frame pointer); a stub per loop header writes them and calls\nthe body, whose prologue for that header loads the live-ins from the\nframe and jumps to the header. A live-in a loop entry loads is a\nCranelift variable, defined at its own definition and at each\nprologue, so the frontend merges the paths at the header; constants\nan entry would rebuild are defined once at the function's entry\ninstead, so they stay immediates. The normal entry pays one load and\na predicted branch. Cold-loop exits check the entry kind at run time,\nsince only an interpreter-entered activation has a frame to resume.\n\nRemoved with it: OsrSelect and the staged compile, the OsrEntries\ninstall path, the module-body stub and wren_run_interpreted,\nhot_header and request_tier_up_at.\n\nMac: the module body's baseline compile 8.6 + 1.7 ms -\u003e 4.0 ms;\nmethod_call 22.5 -\u003e 21.8 ms. NUC: 23 ms either way; tally kernels in\nthe baseline tier within noise of before (setter 2.51 -\u003e 2.73, method\n3.42 -\u003e 3.19), tiered unchanged. A first attempt that made the\nrebuilt constants variables too turned them into loop-carried block\nparameters and cost 10-25% in the baseline tier.","files":null}]}